          <hr class="essay-divider" />

          <h2>What &ldquo;CRITICAL&rdquo; means and what it doesn&rsquo;t</h2>

          <p>
            CRITICAL = sole maintainer + &gt;10M weekly downloads. That&rsquo;s the structural profile
            shared by ua-parser-js before October 2021 (sole maintainer, ~8M/wk, credentials compromised,
            malicious versions published &mdash; CVE-2021-41265/CVE-2021-41266). Same profile as axios
            in March 2026 (100M/wk, sole maintainer, North Korea-linked group UNC1069 via stolen npm token).
          </p>

          <p>
            What it doesn&rsquo;t mean: that the maintainer is careless, or that the package will be
            attacked. Isaac Z. Schlueter has maintained some of these packages for over a decade.
            They&rsquo;re excellent software. The risk is structural, not personal &mdash; one person&rsquo;s
            credentials are the only barrier between 340 million weekly installs and a malicious publish.
          </p>

          <p>
            <code>npm audit</code> showed zero issues on axios for its entire history. The structural
            signal existed before the attack. It just wasn&rsquo;t surfaced.
          </p>

          <hr class="essay-divider" />

          <h2>Check your own lock file</h2>

